{
  "_readme": [
    "Weather stations for the HillTrek Weather Station feed (wx-stations.json).",
    "",
    "THE FIRST FIVE ARE THE APP'S OWN LIST, COPIED VERBATIM from wx.js PLACES —",
    "same names, same coordinates, same elevations. Do not 'correct' them against",
    "a gazetteer: they are what the wall tablet has been showing, and changing a",
    "coordinate here silently changes what that device reports. Note that the",
    "app's 'Cathedral Peak' sits near the hotel/camp rather than the summit; that",
    "is deliberate and shipped.",
    "",
    "Everything after them was taken from tiles.hilltrek.co.za/places_za.json and",
    "checked to fall inside the Drakensberg box (lat -30.4..-28.3, lon 28.4..29.9).",
    "That check is not decoration: the gazetteer holds same-named places all over",
    "the country, and a naive first-match put 'Kamberg' in the Eastern Cape and",
    "'Bushman's Castle' in the Western Cape. fetch_wx_stations.py re-validates the",
    "box at runtime and refuses to publish a station outside it.",
    "",
    "'ele' is the real ground elevation and is null where no trustworthy figure",
    "was available — it is NOT invented. The script fills 'model_ele' from met.no's",
    "own model topography, which is typically far lower than a summit (met.no",
    "models the point above at 1533 m). Keeping both makes that gap visible",
    "instead of quietly presenting a valley forecast as a summit one."
  ],
